WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:07.589
in your work you you quote Nietzsche
quite a bit his a line "he who has a why

00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:14.183
to live for can bear almost any how". What do you think he meant by that?

00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:15.990
What I think that..?

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:22.670
What you think he meant by that? The same as
I'm intended to convey to my readers and

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:30.029
students: that the vision of a meaning
ahead of someone, a meaning in wait for

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:37.710
someone to be fulfilled by someone, that
this contributes most than anything else

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:46.860
under equal other circumstances for
survival. Meaning is the most important

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:54.809
thing in our lives? Certainly because a
what I call a "will to meaning" - the wish

00:00:54.809 --> 00:01:01.770
to find and to fulfill meaning is the
basic motivation in human beings.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:08.250
This certainly runs counter to much of
the determinist notions that are being

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:13.200
bandied around these days that
man is a machine man is a computer man

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:19.939
is a product of instincts. Man is
something like a rat in experiments

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:26.909
psychological experiments. Of course you
are right but not only against the

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:33.960
so called deterministic concepts of man but
also regarding the motivational theories

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:40.280
of certain psychotherapeutic systems.
Let's talk for a minute about

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.579
logotherapy
which arose out of this notion of a

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:52.470
search for meaning. Logotherapy, as one
among other types of psychotherapy, is

00:01:52.470 --> 00:02:01.020
we may say a "meaning centered" psychotherapy
in as much particularly as logotherapy

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:09.119
sees a human being not predominantly
determined, not to say dominated by the

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:12.870
will to pleasure as you were mentioning, nor

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:18.590
by the will to power along the lines of
Adlerian teachings, but basically

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:26.819
fundamentally by a will to meaning.
That is to say the desire, the impulse to

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:33.390
find to discover in life or better to
say in each life situation, concrete life

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:39.239
situation confronting someone, the desire
to find a meaning therein and

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:43.379
to go on to fulfill it. I was very
intrigued one of the most surprising

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:51.180
things I've read recently was that you
said that when you talk to European

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:58.489
students only 40 percent said they had
suffered this sort of inner void and yet

00:02:58.489 --> 00:03:03.359
eighty-one percent of American students
experience the same thing.

00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:06.900
We think of it just the opposite,
we think of the Europeans as being

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:14.609
buried under this existential dread and
sense of purposelessness and Americans

00:03:14.609 --> 00:03:19.410
is being optimistic and upbeat.
However it might be, whether the ones or

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:26.639
the others are suffering more
or less respectively from this

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:34.200
existential vacuum, the ones who seem to
suffer less should not look at the

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:43.470
others with contempt but look at the
others with compassion and look for

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:51.690
anything possible to help the others. Now
this void manifests itself as in apathy

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:59.910
in boredom, lack of initiative,
lack of interest - interest in the world

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:07.250
or initiative in changing something
within the world for the better. This

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:17.340
frustration is a a proof of the
existence of a will to meaning. Unless we

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:22.229
were imbued by a will to meaning by the
wish to find meaning and discuss

00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:26.230
discover and fulfill meaning in life
we never

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:32.050
would be able to experience an inner
void so this is in a way also something

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:35.290
positive.
Now you've listed three types of values

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:39.790
creative values, experiential values and
attitudinal variants. You may find a

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:44.770
meaning the "average" man, the man on the
street or the woman on the street may

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:53.560
find a meaning day by day in doing a
deed in creating a work and - that's the

00:04:53.560 --> 00:05:02.110
creative - creative and in experiencing
something. The beauty. The truth as a

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:09.130
researcher, or the good in dealing with
people as a teacher or whatsoever. There's an

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:13.540
extraordinary moment in "man's search for
meaning" when you talk about being in one

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:19.540
of the one of the Nazi camps and all of
you going out to look at a sunset. Is

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:26.650
that experiential? Exactly this is a paradigm of
experiential values, of finding a meaning

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:31.240
in experiencing without doing anything
without achieving or accomplishing

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:37.840
anything but just in giving oneself the
immediate experience of something say

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:44.140
beautiful going on in the world. This is
the second avenue but there is also

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:54.370
another aspect of experiential
values. Excuse me, not only experiencing

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:59.820
something but also experiencing someone.
More than that, experiencing

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:06.250
another human being in his
or her very uniqueness and it is the

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:14.500
main attribute of a human being that he
is a person in contrast to any animal he

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:20.820
is a person a person is always something
absolutely unique irreparable in the

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:26.140
evolution of the cosmos as is we are
incomparable with any other human being

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:34.930
and this uniqueness can be got hold of
solely by a loving person, Because he not

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:40.329
only sees the essence but also the
potentials in the beloved person

00:06:40.329 --> 00:06:46.329
thereby as I put it before promoting him
alleviating it to reach out to attain

00:06:46.329 --> 00:06:53.199
this potential and to fulfill and
thereby actualize also himself but not

00:06:53.199 --> 00:06:57.549
by preaching self-actualization. It's
nonsense

00:06:57.549 --> 00:07:03.939
self-actualization can only fall into
your lap automatically once that you

00:07:03.939 --> 00:07:10.059
have fulfilled a concrete meaning, done
the best of a situation. Then you actualize

00:07:10.059 --> 00:07:14.979
yourself as a by-product. Let's talk
about the third set of values which is

00:07:14.979 --> 00:07:23.379
the attitudinal, the idea of choosing how
to respond to suffering.

00:07:23.379 --> 00:07:31.619
Choosing the attitude - yes. If there is no
possibility in a given situation to

00:07:31.619 --> 00:07:37.959
fulfill the meaning of a situation by
giving oneself to the experience of

00:07:37.959 --> 00:07:42.819
beauty and so forth. Nor if you have lost the

00:07:42.819 --> 00:07:49.179
capability to do your job to do your
work even then there is an ultimate

00:07:49.179 --> 00:07:55.089
possibility to find and
fulfill meaning - not only the ultimate it

00:07:55.089 --> 00:08:03.369
is even the potential to fulfill the
deepest meaning, to attain the highest values:

00:08:03.369 --> 00:08:11.019
by your approach to the given situation, a tragic

00:08:11.019 --> 00:08:17.759
or trist situation confronting you. You said
that in part of the initial shock of

00:08:17.759 --> 00:08:24.249
being put in a death camp was there was
was ultimately an acceptance that we

00:08:24.249 --> 00:08:29.319
knew we had nothing to lose
except our ridiculously naked lives is

00:08:29.319 --> 00:08:35.110
that the situation that they're in? - In
a way - Is this when you

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:41.559
make the choice of how you go into..
your last value choices how to react to

00:08:41.559 --> 00:08:47.410
the situation? You stand there, you stood
there naked with nothing you could have

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:52.940
had but all the more what counted and
the mattered was what

00:08:52.940 --> 00:09:04.130
you were - "being" rather than "having",
possessing anything. So what

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:11.330
counted was what you make out of this
situation, what attitude you adopt

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:17.600
in the given situation and there is a
multitude a wealth of possible attitudes

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:24.140
to how to approach it. So we have to
decide. The ultimate I would take it

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:33.020
attitudinal value challenge that we all share
is how we're going to face death. How do

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:36.530
you prepare people for that? How do you
prepare yourself for that?

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:43.900
I couldn't prepare anyone else unless I would have prepared myself

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:51.080
because if you are a psychiatrist
your patients feel exactly whether or

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:58.430
not you are really convinced of what you
are teaching and telling them. Now I'm

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:06.340
convinced that in contrast to the usual
aspect or be it sound aspect to life and

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:13.730
more specifically to the
past, to life's transitoriness and this

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:20.380
includes that we approach, each of us are
approaching death, in contrast to that I

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:28.690
maintain that in the past nothing is
lost but right on the contrary

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:36.170
everything is stored forever.
It is not annihilated by transitoriness

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:43.820
but on the contrary it has been, it is
becoming preserved forever. Something you

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:49.790
have done can never be undone. Something
you have experienced something you have

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:55.370
even experienced in a negative sense
going through suffering and if for

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:58.720
instance you suffered, gone through this
suffering

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:05.600
honestly courageously and with dignity
who in the world, what what in the world

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.410
can deny it,
can annihilate this? What you have done

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:15.560
has been done forever
in both ways in a negative as in a

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:23.259
positive way, it cannot be
undone. And the past is a storehouse of

00:11:23.259 --> 00:11:28.009
what you have done what you have
experienced what you have gone through

00:11:28.009 --> 00:11:35.569
and what you have done out of all the
negative and tragic aspects as even

00:11:35.569 --> 00:11:38.959
encountered within your life. I want to
thank you for being on the show

00:11:38.959 --> 00:11:42.250
and I want to thank you at home for
watching.

